Alembic migration environment for whisperX-FastAPI.

The database URL is not configured in alembic.ini — alembic/env.py uses the
application's own sync engine, which is built from DB_URL. Set DB_URL (or the
.env file) the same way you would for running the app.

Common commands:

    uv run alembic upgrade head        # apply all pending migrations
    uv run alembic downgrade -1        # revert the most recent migration
    uv run alembic current             # show the revision the database is at
    uv run alembic history             # list revisions

To add a migration after changing app/infrastructure/database/models.py:

    uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"

Always read the generated revision before committing it — autogenerate does not
detect every change (notably column renames, which it emits as a drop plus an
add, losing the data).
